      "text": "Go in unto thy brother’s wife, and marry her, Gen. 38:8. Ye shall not afflict any widow, Ex. 22:22. judgment of the fatherless and widow, Deut. 10:18. fatherless, and the widow … shall come, and shall eat, Deut. 14:29. hast forgot a sheaf … it shall be for … the widow, Deut. 24:19. wife of the dead shall not marry … stranger, Deut. 25:5. Ruth … the wife of the dead, Ruth 4:5. a widow woman there to sustain thee, 1 Kgs. 17:9. judge of the widows, is God, Ps. 68:5. They slay the widow and the stranger, Ps. 94:6. his children be fatherless, and his wife a widow, Ps. 109:9. Lord … relieveth the fatherless and widow, Ps. 146:9. Lord … will establish the border of the widow, Prov. 15:25. plead for the widow, Isa. 1:17. not remember the reproach of thy widowhood any more, Isa. 54:4. let thy widows trust in me, Jer. 49:11. oppress not the widow, Zech. 7:10.",
